1
00:00:00,001 --> 00:00:01,458
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,460 --> 00:00:03,001
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:11,803 --> 00:00:13,585
It's dystonia.

4
00:00:13,793 --> 00:00:15,483
You said you play the cello, right?

5
00:00:16,035 --> 00:00:17,035
Yes.

6
00:00:17,043 --> 00:00:19,460
It's pretty common among musicians.

7
00:00:19,501 --> 00:00:21,918
It's also known as musician's cramp.

8
00:00:22,460 --> 00:00:25,043
You should stop playing for a while...

9
00:00:25,293 --> 00:00:26,751
and get some treatment.

10
00:00:27,418 --> 00:00:28,418
I can't.

11
00:00:28,793 --> 00:00:31,001
I need to teach lessons to make a living.

12
00:00:50,376 --> 00:00:54,626
(My Biggest Fan, Sa Bin)

13
00:01:17,339 --> 00:01:18,339
(Episode 33)

14
00:01:18,342 --> 00:01:20,092
- Congratulations, sir.
- Congratulations.

15
00:01:20,960 --> 00:01:22,043
That's enough.

16
00:01:22,126 --> 00:01:24,293
Thank you so much. It's all thanks to you.

17
00:01:24,335 --> 00:01:25,666
I met with the CEO this morning,

18
00:01:25,668 --> 00:01:27,835
and he said no other team
could've pulled off this schedule.

19
00:01:28,001 --> 00:01:29,541
You worked so hard.

20
00:01:29,543 --> 00:01:32,291
You stayed up all night with me.
I should be thanking you.

21
00:01:32,293 --> 00:01:34,751
- Well, if you insist...
- We'll take you up on that.

22
00:01:34,793 --> 00:01:36,418
How about I book us lunch?

23
00:01:36,960 --> 00:01:38,710
Sure. It's on me.

24
00:01:39,085 --> 00:01:40,541
- Let's go to that steakhouse again.
- Sounds good.

25
00:01:40,543 --> 00:01:41,751
Let's go to the steakhouse.

26
00:01:48,168 --> 00:01:49,293
Are you having a hard time?

27
00:01:50,751 --> 00:01:51,876
Is it lunchtime already?

28
00:01:52,261 --> 00:01:53,624
I'm having lunch with the staff.

29
00:01:53,626 --> 00:01:54,626
They're celebrating with me.

30
00:01:54,659 --> 00:01:56,659
Yeah, I heard. Are you getting promoted?

31
00:01:56,668 --> 00:01:57,710
It's more than I deserve.

32
00:01:58,335 --> 00:02:00,960
- I guess...
- Ambassador Do must've helped you out.

33
00:02:01,251 --> 00:02:02,710
Of course, you earned it too.

34
00:02:02,751 --> 00:02:04,418
I'm getting more credit than I deserve.

35
00:02:05,626 --> 00:02:07,460
Dad, what should I do about this?

36
00:02:07,835 --> 00:02:09,583
People at the center don't say anything,

37
00:02:09,585 --> 00:02:10,835
but they know what's going on.

38
00:02:11,335 --> 00:02:13,501
People in other departments
aren't even subtle about it.

39
00:02:15,126 --> 00:02:16,876
Of course they all know.

40
00:02:18,626 --> 00:02:19,835
Try not to worry about it.

41
00:02:20,418 --> 00:02:21,418
"Not worry about it?"

42
00:02:21,424 --> 00:02:23,001
No matter how much you deny it,

43
00:02:23,293 --> 00:02:25,876
once you're on the same team as Do Hee,
people are bound to talk.

44
00:02:26,376 --> 00:02:27,960
Give it some time.

45
00:02:28,085 --> 00:02:30,376
How long can Ambassador Do
keep looking out for you?

46
00:02:31,026 --> 00:02:32,109
Not forever.

47
00:02:33,043 --> 00:02:34,626
Build up your skills in the meantime.

48
00:02:34,918 --> 00:02:38,126
Even if Ambassador Do retires,
if you do well, won't that prove it?

49
00:02:39,041 --> 00:02:40,597
I don't see it that way.

50
00:02:40,793 --> 00:02:41,960
It must be upsetting.

51
00:02:42,918 --> 00:02:46,168
You must feel frustrated that your efforts
are overshadowed by your in-laws.

52
00:02:46,719 --> 00:02:48,136
But you're surprising me, Dad.

53
00:02:48,626 --> 00:02:50,126
I thought you'd tell me to turn it down.

54
00:02:50,168 --> 00:02:51,876
That's why you came all the way here.

55
00:02:52,219 --> 00:02:54,261
If I told you to turn it down, would you?

56
00:02:54,751 --> 00:02:56,835
- Yes.
- Your mom likes it.

57
00:02:58,276 --> 00:03:00,442
Looks like Do Hee stopped by this morning.

58
00:03:00,543 --> 00:03:02,124
Where do you find girls like her
these days?

59
00:03:02,126 --> 00:03:04,793
Most people get even more arrogant
when they come from a powerful family.

60
00:03:05,540 --> 00:03:07,915
Would you have said the same thing
back then, Dad?

61
00:03:07,918 --> 00:03:09,835
I do whatever makes your mom happy.

62
00:03:12,322 --> 00:03:13,364
You really are something, Dad.

63
00:03:13,918 --> 00:03:15,418
I'll go see my uncle before I leave.

64
00:03:46,168 --> 00:03:47,168
Yeong Ju.

65
00:04:03,220 --> 00:04:06,095
I felt like I was fighting
the whole world.

66
00:04:07,394 --> 00:04:09,060
After my husband abandoned me,

67
00:04:09,751 --> 00:04:12,126
everyone felt sorry for me at first.

68
00:04:12,876 --> 00:04:15,335
Having everyone around me
know about my misfortune...

69
00:04:16,852 --> 00:04:18,518
was humiliating.

70
00:04:19,460 --> 00:04:22,585
It must've been hard to bear
at such a young age.

71
00:04:26,010 --> 00:04:29,135
They started telling me to get divorced,
asking why I was holding on.

72
00:04:30,335 --> 00:04:34,510
Even my mother-in-law
initially cursed my husband,

73
00:04:36,001 --> 00:04:38,626
but before long, she started blaming me.

74
00:04:39,918 --> 00:04:41,168
That's unbelievable.

75
00:04:42,317 --> 00:04:44,401
It was one unbelievable thing
after another.

76
00:04:45,126 --> 00:04:47,918
"Divorce him." "Don't let him go."

77
00:04:48,626 --> 00:04:51,251
"Your stubbornness
drove your husband away."

78
00:04:54,501 --> 00:04:58,793
I don't understand why everyone else
gets to decide my life.

79
00:05:01,885 --> 00:05:02,885
Yeong Ju.

80
00:05:05,392 --> 00:05:07,392
I've finally found peace.

81
00:05:08,335 --> 00:05:10,760
I don't want to go back
into the storm ever again.

82
00:05:11,585 --> 00:05:14,793
Why do you think being with me
would mean going into a storm?

83
00:05:16,001 --> 00:05:19,376
I'm older, and I've been married before.

84
00:05:20,543 --> 00:05:22,001
I'm a grandmother too.

85
00:05:22,876 --> 00:05:24,883
Your brother and his wife...

86
00:05:25,835 --> 00:05:27,501
might have a hard time accepting me.

87
00:05:28,126 --> 00:05:31,231
I'll take care of that.

88
00:05:31,626 --> 00:05:33,168
That's exactly what I don't want.

89
00:05:33,293 --> 00:05:35,876
I don't want to be treated
like some woman with a tragic past again.

90
00:05:38,710 --> 00:05:40,210
I'm going to keep living like this.

91
00:05:40,710 --> 00:05:42,001
As for you,

92
00:05:42,751 --> 00:05:45,210
you should find someone
who's right for you.

93
00:05:45,342 --> 00:05:48,301
Why should you decide who's right for me?

94
00:05:48,710 --> 00:05:50,293
I told you before.

95
00:05:51,293 --> 00:05:53,126
I fell in love with you
after I came to admire you.

96
00:05:53,793 --> 00:05:56,501
Why do you keep saying you admire me?

97
00:05:56,793 --> 00:05:58,168
There's nothing admirable about me.

98
00:05:58,293 --> 00:05:59,758
The life you've lived.

99
00:06:01,293 --> 00:06:03,835
You don't realize how much you shine
when you're teaching singing, do you?

100
00:06:05,251 --> 00:06:07,626
That comes from the life you've lived.

101
00:06:09,210 --> 00:06:13,126
Your smile is even more beautiful
because you know what sadness is.

102
00:06:15,418 --> 00:06:17,043
That's not who you are, Yeong Ju.

103
00:06:21,751 --> 00:06:23,749
(Boyak Oriental Medicine Clinic)

104
00:06:23,751 --> 00:06:25,083
(Temporarily Closed Due to Circumstances)

105
00:06:25,085 --> 00:06:27,626
Uncle, you'll never find
a love like this again.

106
00:06:27,751 --> 00:06:29,543
Just go for it.

107
00:06:29,993 --> 00:06:31,951
It's the love you found after 50 years.

108
00:06:34,202 --> 00:06:36,541
Come on, don't be afraid.

109
00:06:36,543 --> 00:06:38,541
Just go straight to your brother
and face him head-on.

110
00:06:38,543 --> 00:06:40,335
Is my dad a wall?
Why would he run into him?

111
00:06:41,960 --> 00:06:44,293
We're here to find a way to persuade him.

112
00:06:44,418 --> 00:06:46,335
She's older than him.

113
00:06:47,043 --> 00:06:49,168
That doesn't matter. It's just...

114
00:06:50,085 --> 00:06:52,106
I don't know if she really...

115
00:06:52,274 --> 00:06:54,291
is uncomfortable with my love, or if...

116
00:06:54,293 --> 00:06:55,708
she feels the same way I do,

117
00:06:55,710 --> 00:06:59,251
but is turning me down
because of our circumstances.

118
00:07:01,592 --> 00:07:04,842
I want to do whatever she wants,
whatever is best for her.

119
00:07:04,918 --> 00:07:08,208
Uncle, are you always this over-the-top?

120
00:07:08,210 --> 00:07:10,126
Be quiet.

121
00:07:12,043 --> 00:07:13,822
Are you absolutely sure
about how you feel?

122
00:07:14,251 --> 00:07:16,122
If you give up halfway,
you'll hurt her again.

123
00:07:16,124 --> 00:07:17,270
You need to be sure.

124
00:07:17,295 --> 00:07:18,351
And once you decide,

125
00:07:18,354 --> 00:07:20,082
you have to see it through, as Tae O said.
You can't back down.

126
00:07:20,085 --> 00:07:22,291
The fact that you're thinking
this hard about it...

127
00:07:22,293 --> 00:07:24,293
really surprises me.

128
00:07:25,001 --> 00:07:27,354
Now I'm curious about this grandma.

129
00:07:27,710 --> 00:07:29,783
I think I'm sure about how I feel,

130
00:07:30,367 --> 00:07:32,700
but I don't even know myself that well.

131
00:07:33,376 --> 00:07:36,251
What do you think?
Do you think I'm 100 percent sure?

132
00:07:36,751 --> 00:07:38,168
Can I trust myself?

133
00:07:38,960 --> 00:07:39,960
I'm not sure.

134
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:41,999
Trust yourself.

135
00:07:42,001 --> 00:07:44,501
If you don't trust yourself, who will?

136
00:07:44,793 --> 00:07:45,960
Can I really do that?

137
00:07:46,126 --> 00:07:49,600
I've never seen such indecisive men
in my life.

138
00:07:50,335 --> 00:07:52,501
Then make your decision
at the 70th birthday celebration.

139
00:07:52,504 --> 00:07:54,999
It's an important decision.
It's not just about him.

140
00:07:55,001 --> 00:07:56,208
At the end of the day, it's just life.

141
00:07:56,210 --> 00:07:57,710
And he's already lived 50 years.

142
00:07:57,751 --> 00:07:59,833
He's deciding how to spend
the next 30 years. What's there to fear?

143
00:07:59,835 --> 00:08:02,418
If he lets this chance slip away,
do you think he'll get another one?

144
00:08:03,168 --> 00:08:06,251
Come on. In times like this,
you just go for it.

145
00:08:06,376 --> 00:08:08,501
Uncle, go for it. No matter what.

146
00:08:11,034 --> 00:08:12,733
"No matter what?"

147
00:08:36,251 --> 00:08:39,085
I felt like I was fighting
the whole world.

148
00:08:40,210 --> 00:08:41,950
After my husband abandoned me,

149
00:08:42,585 --> 00:08:45,043
everyone felt sorry for me at first.

150
00:08:48,418 --> 00:08:50,376
I've finally found peace.

151
00:08:51,376 --> 00:08:53,751
I don't want to go back
into the storm ever again.

152
00:09:12,210 --> 00:09:14,751
You don't realize how much you shine
when you're teaching singing, do you?

153
00:09:15,634 --> 00:09:17,843
That comes from the life you've lived.

154
00:09:18,234 --> 00:09:22,151
Your smile is even more beautiful
because you know what sadness is.

155
00:09:24,126 --> 00:09:25,668
That's not who you are, Yeong Ju.

156
00:09:30,876 --> 00:09:32,183
Shining, my foot.

157
00:09:33,668 --> 00:09:35,501
He's got a knack for sweet-talking people.

158
00:09:56,543 --> 00:09:57,751
What's going on?

159
00:09:57,835 --> 00:09:59,308
Why are you scaring us like this?

160
00:10:00,126 --> 00:10:02,085
What is it? Is O Reum sick?

161
00:10:02,168 --> 00:10:04,251
Mom, would he be smiling like that
if he were sick?

162
00:10:04,335 --> 00:10:05,626
Mai, what is it? Hurry up and tell us.

163
00:10:05,751 --> 00:10:08,662
Mom, O Reum's going
to have a little sibling.

164
00:10:11,441 --> 00:10:14,075
I thought the stock market
had gone up or something.

165
00:10:14,085 --> 00:10:16,668
Hey, O Reum's sibling
is worth more than stocks.

166
00:10:17,293 --> 00:10:18,626
It has nothing to do with me.

167
00:10:19,168 --> 00:10:20,691
You're jealous.

168
00:10:20,960 --> 00:10:23,354
- Right?
- Not really.

169
00:10:24,918 --> 00:10:26,126
That's good news.

170
00:10:26,293 --> 00:10:28,343
We finally get some good news
after all that trouble.

171
00:10:28,710 --> 00:10:30,270
Take good care of yourself,

172
00:10:30,626 --> 00:10:33,656
and don't go clubbing while pregnant
like you did with O Reum.

173
00:10:34,126 --> 00:10:35,335
Okay.

174
00:10:39,460 --> 00:10:42,376
What? Should I congratulate you too?

175
00:10:42,460 --> 00:10:45,960
Fine. I hope you have a healthy baby
and take good care of them.

176
00:10:50,751 --> 00:10:53,835
- Too loud.
- Really?

177
00:10:54,335 --> 00:10:56,210
Was I too loud, sweetheart?

178
00:10:57,418 --> 00:11:00,335
O Reum, there's some very good news.

179
00:11:00,460 --> 00:11:02,791
You're going to be a big brother.

180
00:11:02,793 --> 00:11:04,249
There's a baby in your mom's tummy.

181
00:11:04,251 --> 00:11:05,335
Really?

182
00:11:06,085 --> 00:11:08,126
It's true, little man.

183
00:11:08,918 --> 00:11:11,210
There'll be four of us.

184
00:11:12,418 --> 00:11:14,168
Let me see the baby.

185
00:11:19,168 --> 00:11:20,376
Are you happy?

186
00:11:31,075 --> 00:11:33,239
I used to wish O Reum had a sibling,

187
00:11:33,399 --> 00:11:34,992
so we could save him,

188
00:11:36,334 --> 00:11:37,834
and now we're actually having one.

189
00:11:38,751 --> 00:11:40,835
We all had the same thought.

190
00:11:41,710 --> 00:11:43,960
Why? Are you embarrassed?

191
00:11:44,960 --> 00:11:45,960
A little.

192
00:11:46,460 --> 00:11:48,001
Don't be ridiculous.

193
00:11:48,126 --> 00:11:49,912
Your baby can hear you.

194
00:11:50,335 --> 00:11:53,866
Haven't you heard of wartime baby booms?

195
00:11:55,210 --> 00:11:57,418
Korea went through one too.

196
00:11:57,960 --> 00:11:59,001
Really?

197
00:11:59,710 --> 00:12:01,043
You're a married couple.

198
00:12:01,126 --> 00:12:02,802
Don't overthink it.

199
00:12:03,001 --> 00:12:05,095
You're not having an affair,
so why be embarrassed?

200
00:12:05,960 --> 00:12:08,626
What do you mean, an affair?

201
00:12:08,710 --> 00:12:10,566
Does love need a label?

202
00:12:10,876 --> 00:12:12,333
Do you think the love you have now...

203
00:12:12,335 --> 00:12:14,335
is more mature than your first love?

204
00:12:14,835 --> 00:12:16,643
All love is childish,

205
00:12:16,645 --> 00:12:18,708
reckless, and happens in an instant.

206
00:12:19,001 --> 00:12:20,924
Mother, are you really dating?

207
00:12:21,085 --> 00:12:22,629
No, of course not.

208
00:12:22,918 --> 00:12:24,970
Stop talking nonsense around the kids.

209
00:12:25,168 --> 00:12:27,249
I don't lose my head over love like you.

210
00:12:27,251 --> 00:12:29,751
I have a family and a position to protect.

211
00:12:30,501 --> 00:12:32,918
Don't be surprised. It's nonsense.

212
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:37,626
Is she really dating?

213
00:12:39,001 --> 00:12:40,291
I'm not sure yet.

214
00:12:40,293 --> 00:12:43,545
She seems unsure whether
to let herself fall for him.

215
00:12:43,960 --> 00:12:45,418
Can anyone control that?

216
00:12:45,585 --> 00:12:47,499
Like you said,

217
00:12:47,501 --> 00:12:48,793
don't you just fall in love?

218
00:12:48,835 --> 00:12:49,960
That's my point.

219
00:12:50,825 --> 00:12:51,833
Second Mother.

220
00:12:51,835 --> 00:12:54,043
Stop calling me that.

221
00:12:55,001 --> 00:12:56,758
Still better than "ma'am."

222
00:12:57,710 --> 00:13:01,126
- Where did you buy this?
- Hey, be careful.

223
00:13:02,585 --> 00:13:05,291
My husband got it for me
during our honeymoon in Europe.

224
00:13:05,293 --> 00:13:06,958
You can't find one anymore.

225
00:13:06,960 --> 00:13:08,125
Father bought it?

226
00:13:08,293 --> 00:13:10,126
And he didn't buy one for mother?

227
00:13:10,585 --> 00:13:12,668
That's the privilege of being loved.

228
00:13:17,334 --> 00:13:19,334
That's really getting on my nerves.

229
00:13:23,200 --> 00:13:24,909
I keep getting hot, then cold...

230
00:13:25,710 --> 00:13:27,543
It must be menopause.

231
00:13:41,029 --> 00:13:42,960
Are you seriously going to talk nonsense
in front of the kids?

232
00:13:43,001 --> 00:13:44,458
Do you want me to kick you out?

233
00:13:44,460 --> 00:13:47,918
You still get your period.
Why hesitate? Just go for it.

234
00:13:48,376 --> 00:13:50,624
That doesn't mean I'm encouraging you.

235
00:13:50,626 --> 00:13:52,376
It didn't sound encouraging to me.

236
00:13:53,043 --> 00:13:56,168
You want my kids to think I've lost it?

237
00:13:56,585 --> 00:13:57,585
Yes.

238
00:13:59,668 --> 00:14:00,668
Yeong Ju.

239
00:14:00,891 --> 00:14:04,331
Young love is naive,
and old love is embarrassing.

240
00:14:04,835 --> 00:14:07,416
Isn't it ridiculous to label love...

241
00:14:07,501 --> 00:14:08,918
according to how old you are?

242
00:14:09,501 --> 00:14:12,876
Haven't you seen the play
"Harold and Maude?"

243
00:14:13,668 --> 00:14:17,626
Love makes you shy,
whether you're 19 or 80.

244
00:14:17,710 --> 00:14:22,210
Listen, I found out this morning
I'm getting a second grandchild.

245
00:14:22,751 --> 00:14:25,079
- Are you happy?
- Of course I am.

246
00:14:25,418 --> 00:14:27,418
You'll understand
when Ji Ni gets pregnant someday.

247
00:14:27,501 --> 00:14:29,841
Grandchildren are nothing
like children of your own.

248
00:14:29,918 --> 00:14:32,395
I don't think that'll happen for me.

249
00:14:33,085 --> 00:14:35,251
She bolts whenever I bring up marriage.

250
00:14:36,043 --> 00:14:38,993
She says watching me put her off love.

251
00:14:40,835 --> 00:14:42,876
I guess that's my punishment too.

252
00:14:43,710 --> 00:14:46,793
I thought Ji Ni was quite popular.

253
00:14:47,251 --> 00:14:50,376
She is. She just won't let anyone in.

254
00:14:51,918 --> 00:14:54,918
I can take the whole world judging me,

255
00:14:55,126 --> 00:14:58,304
but it hurts when my own daughter does it.

256
00:15:03,509 --> 00:15:05,708
What should I make with these?

257
00:15:12,626 --> 00:15:13,960
You're finally awake.

258
00:15:14,043 --> 00:15:15,043
Yeah.

259
00:15:15,293 --> 00:15:16,624
Who brought me home yesterday?

260
00:15:16,626 --> 00:15:18,100
- Was it Tae O?
- Yes.

261
00:15:18,210 --> 00:15:19,874
Why do you work yourself so hard?

262
00:15:19,876 --> 00:15:21,333
They barely pay you anything.

263
00:15:21,335 --> 00:15:23,208
I told you, I enjoy my work.

264
00:15:23,210 --> 00:15:24,585
Why do you always talk like that?

265
00:15:25,710 --> 00:15:26,793
Time to eat.

266
00:15:28,043 --> 00:15:29,397
Did you see that?

267
00:15:29,399 --> 00:15:31,814
Have you ever seen a daughter
look at her mom like that?

268
00:15:32,460 --> 00:15:34,831
Yeah, I've seen plenty.

269
00:15:38,768 --> 00:15:40,934
O Reum, I have to go to work now.

270
00:15:41,168 --> 00:15:42,376
Don't go.

271
00:15:45,001 --> 00:15:47,637
Okay. I'll stay five more minutes.

272
00:15:47,918 --> 00:15:50,291
- Great.
- Look at this little guy...

273
00:15:50,293 --> 00:15:52,668
He's holding on to my daughter.

274
00:15:53,376 --> 00:15:55,585
I won't let her go.

275
00:15:56,960 --> 00:15:58,835
You're so cute.

276
00:15:59,626 --> 00:16:02,585
How adorable.

277
00:16:03,376 --> 00:16:04,787
Really?

278
00:16:05,251 --> 00:16:06,251
Yeah.

279
00:16:06,710 --> 00:16:09,516
Too bad I didn't film her in action.

280
00:16:09,751 --> 00:16:12,545
I'm proud to say I saw it in person.

281
00:16:13,626 --> 00:16:15,043
I've seen it a few times.

282
00:16:15,251 --> 00:16:16,251
Really?

283
00:16:17,085 --> 00:16:19,034
Whenever the professor gave her
an assignment out of nowhere,

284
00:16:19,036 --> 00:16:20,777
it was like she had superpowers.

285
00:16:22,009 --> 00:16:24,676
- Still, about the tablet...
- It was Do Hee. A million percent.

286
00:16:24,710 --> 00:16:26,749
Are you that sure? Without any evidence?

287
00:16:26,751 --> 00:16:29,335
This happened several times
when we were in arts high school.

288
00:16:29,617 --> 00:16:31,420
We don't have proof,
but all signs point to her.

289
00:16:31,960 --> 00:16:34,335
We all know Do Hee was behind it.

290
00:16:34,835 --> 00:16:38,376
She'd practically lose her mind
whenever she lost first place.

291
00:16:41,284 --> 00:16:42,701
I'll leave you two to talk.

292
00:16:45,960 --> 00:16:49,001
Wouldn't it be nice
to add music here later?

293
00:16:49,168 --> 00:16:52,333
The kids would love it
if we added percussion.

294
00:16:52,335 --> 00:16:54,710
Later, if the book sells well.

295
00:16:55,543 --> 00:16:57,708
Your mother is a musician, right?

296
00:16:57,710 --> 00:16:59,541
She must have lots of connections.

297
00:16:59,543 --> 00:17:01,043
Maybe we can ask her for help later.

298
00:17:01,543 --> 00:17:03,795
My mom and I are each other's anti-fans.

299
00:17:04,418 --> 00:17:06,960
We became a little closer
after my father passed away,

300
00:17:07,543 --> 00:17:08,793
but she'd probably refuse.

301
00:17:11,668 --> 00:17:14,624
She was worried about you
and took care of you last night.

302
00:17:14,627 --> 00:17:16,211
That's only when people are around.

303
00:17:16,501 --> 00:17:17,793
Want to see something?

304
00:17:20,460 --> 00:17:21,626
Here.

305
00:17:22,918 --> 00:17:24,001
Look at all these.

306
00:17:24,626 --> 00:17:27,918
I've been getting these photos
since I turned 20.

307
00:17:28,751 --> 00:17:31,124
My mom can't wait for my career to fail,

308
00:17:31,126 --> 00:17:33,043
so she can set me up and marry me off.

309
00:17:33,168 --> 00:17:34,902
She'd never agree to help us.

310
00:17:36,876 --> 00:17:38,124
Have you kept all of them?

311
00:17:38,126 --> 00:17:40,835
She denies everything,
so I have to keep the evidence.

312
00:17:41,418 --> 00:17:44,458
But your mother is really cute.

313
00:17:44,460 --> 00:17:46,801
Only because she isn't your mother.

314
00:17:46,960 --> 00:17:48,376
Try living with her.

315
00:17:50,710 --> 00:17:52,888
My mom couldn't marry openly...

316
00:17:53,960 --> 00:17:55,460
- You know that, right?
- Yeah...

317
00:17:57,701 --> 00:17:59,535
You told me about it
when we discussed the transplant.

318
00:17:59,543 --> 00:18:02,210
She thinks I'll be removed
from her family register if I marry.

319
00:18:03,501 --> 00:18:05,918
She sees that as her way
of setting me free.

320
00:18:06,043 --> 00:18:08,751
But I'm completely against marriage.
Like mother, like daughter.

321
00:18:08,960 --> 00:18:11,499
I don't think I'm a lucky person.

322
00:18:11,501 --> 00:18:13,501
Hey, don't say that.

323
00:18:15,210 --> 00:18:16,371
Anyway,

324
00:18:16,664 --> 00:18:19,751
my mom probably won't help us
with the music.

325
00:18:19,876 --> 00:18:23,585
Discuss it with Director Ji Hu
and decide what to do.

326
00:18:23,876 --> 00:18:25,663
Percussion and brass are exciting,

327
00:18:25,666 --> 00:18:27,083
so that's what I recommend.

328
00:18:27,085 --> 00:18:28,793
Okay. Got it.

329
00:18:29,085 --> 00:18:30,335
But seriously...

330
00:18:31,509 --> 00:18:33,842
Do you think Do Hee took the tablet?

331
00:18:34,952 --> 00:18:38,620
It might not have been her.
It could've been a random thief, but...

332
00:18:39,801 --> 00:18:42,715
Jung A and I think it was Do Hee.

333
00:18:48,543 --> 00:18:50,242
- Do Hee.
- So what are you saying?

334
00:18:50,793 --> 00:18:53,083
Ji Ni's tablet went missing,
and you're saying I did it.

335
00:18:53,085 --> 00:18:55,440
So now I'm a criminal
and a thief, is that it?

336
00:18:57,543 --> 00:19:00,085
- That's not what I meant...
- Then what did you mean?

337
00:19:00,335 --> 00:19:01,626
What else could you mean?

338
00:19:01,710 --> 00:19:04,126
Do you think I'm an idiot?

339
00:19:04,168 --> 00:19:05,958
Did you come all this way to tell me that?

340
00:19:05,960 --> 00:19:08,744
Do you have any idea how long it's been
since you came to see me?

341
00:19:09,668 --> 00:19:10,999
This is driving me crazy.

342
00:19:11,001 --> 00:19:12,168
It really wasn't you?

343
00:19:12,335 --> 00:19:14,666
No. I really hope not.

344
00:19:14,668 --> 00:19:17,117
That's why I came all the way here.
I wanted to talk without anyone knowing.

345
00:19:18,510 --> 00:19:19,662
Even back in school,

346
00:19:19,758 --> 00:19:22,210
you'd take the broken-in supplies
and replace them with new ones.

347
00:19:22,418 --> 00:19:24,083
Everyone suspects you.

348
00:19:24,085 --> 00:19:26,208
Jung A, Ji Ni, and Tae O.

349
00:19:26,210 --> 00:19:28,751
What about you?

350
00:19:29,918 --> 00:19:31,085
Forget everyone else.

351
00:19:31,501 --> 00:19:32,708
Just tell me what you think.

352
00:19:32,710 --> 00:19:34,541
I really hope it wasn't you.

353
00:19:34,543 --> 00:19:36,201
How could you even think that?

354
00:19:37,001 --> 00:19:38,293
Na Ji Ni.

355
00:19:38,876 --> 00:19:40,715
I won't let this go.

356
00:19:41,168 --> 00:19:43,541
If it wasn't you, that's all that matters.
What a relief!

357
00:19:43,551 --> 00:19:44,923
Did you really have to check?

358
00:19:45,335 --> 00:19:48,874
Even if there's evidence,
you should say, "It wasn't her. No way."

359
00:19:48,876 --> 00:19:50,249
Isn't that what my boyfriend should do?

360
00:19:50,251 --> 00:19:51,293
I'm sorry.

361
00:19:51,793 --> 00:19:54,043
Things between you and Ji Ni
are pretty complicated,

362
00:19:54,126 --> 00:19:55,168
and this is where we ended up.

363
00:19:57,460 --> 00:20:00,043
Go. I have plans too.

364
00:20:01,210 --> 00:20:02,335
Okay.

365
00:20:02,960 --> 00:20:04,126
I'm really sorry.

366
00:20:15,001 --> 00:20:17,460
Yuja tea? Yuja tea and lemonade.

367
00:20:21,293 --> 00:20:23,255
Boss, could you look over here?

368
00:20:23,335 --> 00:20:24,376
What?

369
00:20:28,967 --> 00:20:30,176
I'll take your order.

370
00:20:45,376 --> 00:20:47,915
Hey, what on earth are you doing?

371
00:20:48,710 --> 00:20:50,417
You said I stole your tablet?

372
00:20:50,543 --> 00:20:53,085
What evidence do you have
to go around saying that?

373
00:20:53,335 --> 00:20:54,751
You bitch!

374
00:20:58,376 --> 00:20:59,458
Let go of me!

375
00:20:59,460 --> 00:21:01,208
Are you seriously crazy?

376
00:21:01,210 --> 00:21:02,210
"Evidence?"

377
00:21:02,876 --> 00:21:04,458
You stole my brushes,

378
00:21:04,460 --> 00:21:06,501
stole my paintings,

379
00:21:08,075 --> 00:21:10,117
and locked me in the storage room
so I couldn't take my exam.

380
00:21:10,710 --> 00:21:12,426
I've been through that countless times.

381
00:21:12,793 --> 00:21:14,501
You did this again, right?

382
00:21:14,668 --> 00:21:15,668
Bring it here.

383
00:21:20,376 --> 00:21:23,611
Back then, you took first place from me,
and I was stuck in second.

384
00:21:23,710 --> 00:21:24,960
Not anymore.

385
00:21:26,168 --> 00:21:28,815
I don't even have to put you down.
You're already broken.

386
00:21:28,876 --> 00:21:30,423
And you look pathetic.

387
00:21:30,768 --> 00:21:31,791
So why would I?

388
00:21:31,793 --> 00:21:34,590
Even when I dropped out of high school,
you still couldn't take first place.

389
00:21:34,709 --> 00:21:36,040
You can't even draw.

390
00:21:36,043 --> 00:21:37,676
- Your drawings suck.
- What?

391
00:21:39,335 --> 00:21:40,960
What? You crazy bitch!

392
00:21:49,751 --> 00:21:52,168
I knew this would happen. Stop it.

393
00:21:52,418 --> 00:21:53,543
Just stop it already.

394
00:21:57,460 --> 00:21:59,543
The two of you against me? How pathetic!

395
00:21:59,960 --> 00:22:02,251
Let's go to the police and prove it.

396
00:22:02,376 --> 00:22:05,501
That's exactly what I want.
Let's finally get to the bottom of this.

397
00:22:05,668 --> 00:22:07,041
Stay out of this.

398
00:22:07,043 --> 00:22:09,499
Why should I? This is my studio.

399
00:22:09,501 --> 00:22:12,416
- Then check the security footage now.
- You had it erased.

400
00:22:12,418 --> 00:22:14,749
I'll file a report with the police.

401
00:22:14,751 --> 00:22:17,166
If they find footage of your car
coming down the main road at that time,

402
00:22:17,168 --> 00:22:20,418
or even footage of you passing
by this building,

403
00:22:21,085 --> 00:22:23,293
then you'll admit you did it. Promise me.

404
00:22:24,960 --> 00:22:27,335
What are you talking about?
Do you own this whole neighborhood?

405
00:22:27,418 --> 00:22:29,585
What does my coming and going
have to do with the tablet?

406
00:22:29,626 --> 00:22:32,124
There has to be footage of me
coming in here and taking it.

407
00:22:32,126 --> 00:22:33,793
You little bitch!

408
00:22:36,543 --> 00:22:38,376
How long are you going
to keep living like this?

409
00:22:40,293 --> 00:22:43,001
You!

410
00:22:45,460 --> 00:22:46,710
Stop it.

411
00:22:50,335 --> 00:22:52,460
Get lost, you mistress's daughter!

412
00:22:56,710 --> 00:22:58,043
You filthy bitch!

413
00:22:58,293 --> 00:22:59,501
You crazy...

414
00:23:03,126 --> 00:23:04,249
Insult me all you want.

415
00:23:04,251 --> 00:23:06,293
I'm not letting words like that
get to me anymore.

416
00:23:06,585 --> 00:23:09,333
That girl who used to tremble
at your words and resent mom and dad...

417
00:23:09,335 --> 00:23:10,543
is gone.

418
00:23:11,001 --> 00:23:13,043
You, product of noble love,

419
00:23:13,251 --> 00:23:14,751
put my tablet back.

420
00:23:17,335 --> 00:23:19,499
That's why I'm saying
we should go to the police.

421
00:23:19,501 --> 00:23:22,126
See for yourselves.

422
00:23:23,210 --> 00:23:26,293
It doesn't matter.
I won't be on the security footage.

423
00:23:33,960 --> 00:23:35,085
You bitch!

424
00:23:36,376 --> 00:23:37,960
What?

425
00:23:52,585 --> 00:23:53,793
What's wrong with her?

426
00:23:57,751 --> 00:23:58,960
Hey, Do Hee...

427
00:24:03,126 --> 00:24:05,501
What are you looking at?
Help me clean this up.

428
00:24:07,918 --> 00:24:09,293
My whole body aches.

429
00:24:09,376 --> 00:24:11,168
Why am I going through this
because of that crazy bitch?

430
00:24:12,301 --> 00:24:13,718
What did you do about the cafe?

431
00:24:13,793 --> 00:24:15,960
The part-time worker showed up.

432
00:24:26,460 --> 00:24:28,085
It's a mess.

433
00:24:30,168 --> 00:24:31,168
Give it to me.

434
00:24:38,751 --> 00:24:39,793
Really?

435
00:24:40,043 --> 00:24:41,472
Yes, Mother.

436
00:24:41,626 --> 00:24:44,376
That girl completely humiliated me today.

437
00:24:47,668 --> 00:24:49,262
She twisted my wrist...

438
00:24:49,293 --> 00:24:52,210
and even slapped me in front of everyone.

439
00:24:53,918 --> 00:24:55,876
What a terrible girl!

440
00:24:56,001 --> 00:24:57,041
Come on, get up.

441
00:24:57,043 --> 00:24:59,543
You need acupuncture and some medicine.

442
00:25:00,001 --> 00:25:03,374
You must've been so scared,
you poor thing.

443
00:25:03,376 --> 00:25:04,876
Mother.

444
00:25:08,918 --> 00:25:12,085
I have no mom to turn to, so I came here.

445
00:25:13,168 --> 00:25:15,460
You did the right thing.

446
00:25:15,626 --> 00:25:18,376
Hey, Do Hee.

447
00:25:18,793 --> 00:25:20,708
Calm down.

448
00:25:20,710 --> 00:25:22,041
I'll take care of everything.

449
00:25:22,043 --> 00:25:24,458
Forget the job.
We can't keep a thug like her...

450
00:25:24,460 --> 00:25:27,126
in Joong Bin's office.

451
00:25:33,751 --> 00:25:36,585
Thank you for understanding.

452
00:25:38,418 --> 00:25:39,999
By the way,

453
00:25:40,001 --> 00:25:42,999
how do girls these days fight like that?

454
00:25:43,001 --> 00:25:44,960
I can't believe this.

455
00:25:45,668 --> 00:25:47,543
She used to do kickboxing.

456
00:25:48,793 --> 00:25:50,683
You got beaten up by someone like that?

457
00:25:51,293 --> 00:25:52,918
Seriously...

458
00:25:53,210 --> 00:25:55,666
Is she trained to be a fighter?

459
00:25:55,668 --> 00:25:57,458
That's scary.

460
00:25:57,460 --> 00:25:59,376
Girls these days are on another level.

461
00:25:59,545 --> 00:26:03,082
Back in our day, we just had
slicked-down bangs and chewed gum.

462
00:26:03,085 --> 00:26:04,085
You poor thing...

463
00:26:05,210 --> 00:26:07,208
You know about that too, Mother?

464
00:26:07,210 --> 00:26:09,166
How could I not know?

465
00:26:09,168 --> 00:26:10,876
It's even in the movies.

466
00:26:11,126 --> 00:26:13,001
- You poor thing...
- Mother.

467
00:26:13,418 --> 00:26:15,501
I shouldn't be saying this,

468
00:26:17,001 --> 00:26:18,708
but she's the daughter of a mistress.

469
00:26:18,710 --> 00:26:22,418
She's insecure, so she learned to fight
and claw her way through life.

470
00:26:23,293 --> 00:26:24,293
"A mistress?"

471
00:26:25,210 --> 00:26:27,958
So her mom was an affair partner?

472
00:26:27,960 --> 00:26:28,960
Yes.

473
00:26:29,251 --> 00:26:31,001
That's why she has so much resentment.

474
00:26:31,418 --> 00:26:33,291
Her mom is a famous cellist.

475
00:26:33,293 --> 00:26:36,168
She never came to school to hide it,
so only her dad did.

476
00:26:36,376 --> 00:26:38,266
So we thought she didn't have a mother.

477
00:26:39,376 --> 00:26:41,085
I don't even know what to say.

478
00:26:44,376 --> 00:26:46,854
But I couldn't tell Ji Hu about her.

479
00:26:47,501 --> 00:26:49,166
I was afraid he'd think I was judging her.

480
00:26:49,168 --> 00:26:51,916
That's not judging her. It's the truth.

481
00:26:51,918 --> 00:26:53,793
He just can't tell...

482
00:26:54,085 --> 00:26:56,335
who he can deal with and who he can't.

483
00:26:56,460 --> 00:26:58,666
Yeah, he's too nice.

484
00:26:58,668 --> 00:26:59,712
Tae O is too.

485
00:27:01,043 --> 00:27:03,710
What could she have learned from her mom?

486
00:27:04,126 --> 00:27:06,874
She probably used her looks
to seduce men...

487
00:27:06,876 --> 00:27:10,585
and pretended to be an artist
just because she could paint a little.

488
00:27:11,043 --> 00:27:12,626
A genius? Hardly.

489
00:27:12,960 --> 00:27:14,168
I know exactly what happened.

490
00:27:15,085 --> 00:27:17,835
Mother, I feel so much better now.

491
00:27:17,876 --> 00:27:19,668
You're no ordinary person.

492
00:27:19,876 --> 00:27:23,043
How dare she lay a hand on you?
You're my daughter-in-law.

493
00:27:23,918 --> 00:27:25,126
It's so frustrating.

494
00:27:45,835 --> 00:27:49,124
(Family Register)

495
00:27:49,126 --> 00:27:50,958
If Yeong Ju had remarried sooner,

496
00:27:50,960 --> 00:27:53,874
I could've taken care of the paperwork,
and she could've been happy too.

497
00:27:53,876 --> 00:27:56,083
Then my daughter and I
wouldn't have had to hear all this.

498
00:27:56,085 --> 00:27:57,916
Find a chance to get her fired.

499
00:27:57,918 --> 00:27:59,249
Are you sure she's Ji Ni's mom?

500
00:27:59,251 --> 00:28:00,374
I realized it again.

501
00:28:00,376 --> 00:28:02,708
I'm just terribly unlucky as a woman.

502
00:28:02,710 --> 00:28:04,208
Is there really no place for me?

503
00:28:04,210 --> 00:28:05,916
There's something important about Sa Bin.

504
00:28:05,918 --> 00:28:07,083
What's wrong with him now?

505
00:28:07,085 --> 00:28:09,085
I think O Reum has a fever.

506
00:28:09,460 --> 00:28:10,501
What?

507
00:28:11,983 --> 00:28:13,983
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
